const Map<String, String> tutorialEn = {
  'tutorial.title': 'Guide',
  'tutorial.intro': 'How to split bills with Fasan Split: scan a receipt, add people, assign items, settle up.',
  'tutorial.idea.title': 'The idea',
  'tutorial.idea.body': 'You photograph the receipt, say who was there and tap who had what. The app calculates everything automatically. There is no account; everything stays on your device until you share it.',
  'tutorial.scan.title': 'Scan a receipt',
  'tutorial.scan.body': 'Tap the plus at the bottom right. Photograph the receipt with the camera, pick a photo or file from the gallery (several at once is fine) or choose “Without receipt” to enter it by hand. The app reads items and total itself.',
  'tutorial.check.title': 'Check',
  'tutorial.check.body': 'Compare total and items with the receipt. The receipt icon at the top shows the photo. Tap an item that is wrong to change it. Everything is saved right away; “Continue later” only closes the bill. The frame of items and bills shows how much is assigned: red open, amber partial, green complete. “Only open items” shows only what is still missing. The list is sorted by status, newest first within it; other sorts and filters are under the filter icon at the top right.',
  'tutorial.assign.title': 'Who was there, who had what',
  'tutorial.assign.body': 'Add the people under “Who was there?”. Pick a person and tap the items they had. If several share an item, assign it to several people. The app works out the shares.',
  'tutorial.paid.title': 'Who paid',
  'tutorial.paid.body': 'Set “Paid by” to the person who laid out the money. That decides who owes whom how much.',
  'tutorial.group.title': 'Create a group',
  'tutorial.group.body': 'Tap “All groups” at the top left. In the window you pick a group or create one with “New group”, for example for a trip or a flat share; the search helps with many groups. With a group picked, the plus starts a new bill that lands right there. You can press and hold a bill and drag it onto “Group” at the bottom. “All” shows everything, “No group” only bills without a group. At the top of the group you see the number of bills, the total and the people. The frame shows how many items are done, in progress or open; the total opens the breakdown. The frame shows bills, total and people, also for “All groups”. The buttons below count items (done, in progress, open) and bills without a payer; tap one to show only those, tap again to switch it off. “Bills | Items” changes the view. Open, Archive and Trash are chosen with the symbol at the top right, sorting and category with the filter symbol, “Select” in the ⋮ menu. In the “Items” view every item looks like in the bill, with the snippet from the receipt; tap it to change it right there. Search finds names, people, items and amounts, remembers your last searches and suggests a fix for typos; a hit opens the bill at that item. Every question mark opens an explanation.',
  'tutorial.invite.title': 'Invite people',
  'tutorial.invite.body': 'Open the group and tap the person icon at the top. Share the link or the code. Whoever opens it is in the group and sees the bills. With “Share live” everyone stays in sync.',
  'tutorial.together.title': 'Enter together',
  'tutorial.together.body': 'In a group anyone can enter for anyone. The app keeps calculating automatically. In the “Settlement” tab you already see who owes whom while you are still entering. You settle up once all bills are entered. To protect something, lock it with the padlock: an item in the item sheet, a whole bill in the menu (⋮). Then only you and the group admin can change it; notes still work. You can write a note on every item and pin a note on every bill; search finds both. A tap in the news leads straight to the bill or the message. If someone enters an item for you only as “maybe”, you get a news entry and decide in the item sheet: “Accept” or “Decline”. Until then it does not count. For others you suggest in the item sheet: “Suggest for someone (maybe)”. Who may enter for you is set per member: tap a member, “May change my shares”: directly, ask first or not allowed. Want to show only some items? Open the item and tap “Send items …”, and they land in the chat as a card.',
  'tutorial.history.title': 'Balance and history',
  'tutorial.history.body': 'In the profile, “How your balance adds up” shows every bill with plus and minus. In the menu (⋮) of a bill, a group and in the profile you find the history: who changed what and how your balance moved. If someone changed a bill, a counter on its thumbnail shows how much, and the bill lists “New since your last visit”. If a shared bill got mixed up, “Bring back an earlier state” at the top of the bill history restores a member\'s last state.',
  'tutorial.settle.title': 'Settle up',
  'tutorial.settle.body': 'Once all bills are in, the people icon at the top of the group shows who pays whom how much. Tap ⋮ on a bill and then “Settle” when it is paid. Settled bills go to the archive. Paid something in between or lent money? In the people window enter it with “Enter a payment or loan”; the balance changes at once.',
  'tutorial.settings.title': 'Settings and backup',
  'tutorial.settings.body': 'There you find appearance, language, performance and this guide. If the app stutters, the “Performance test” under Diagnostics runs a measurement with made-up data and makes a report to share. You open the settings from your profile (picture at the top right), at its top right. In the profile you switch the stand-in: whether others may enter things for you. There you back up your data with “Save a backup”. In the browser, „Check for updates now“ shows the build of your page and reloads it when a newer one exists; your login stays.',
